 "notes": [
  "Calendar: a public Google Calendar (texico@texico.org) embedded on texico.org/calendar, read through its ICS feed (1,404 entries in total, 235 inside the window). Event pages (a JetEngine 'events' post type, 49 pages since 2023) and the news blog (16 posts since Aug 2025) add places and details; the event pages show no dates, so dates come from the calendar or news.",
  "Dropped as non-events: 77 'Offerings:' Sabbath markers, 12 office/school closures, 2 school spring breaks, office Christmas parties, and a 'Stay HOME-Eat Turkey' marker. Recurring internal meetings are listed once with a count (ADCOM, executive committee, office staff meetings, convocation planning meetings, pastoral growth, K-12 board, risk control, EPAC).",
  "The calendar is the most administrative in the union: about half of the remaining entries are committees, boards, staff meetings and union/NAD/GC meetings. No public evangelistic series, health expo or community-service event appears on the calendar or event pages for the window; the only evangelism-related items are the Women's Retreat workshop on phone evangelism (news) and leadership training.",
  "Texico replaced a traditional camp meeting with a one-weekend Convocation (Aug 28-29, 2026, 'In His Presence', Sandia View Academy, Corrales, NM) and a travelling children's summer camp, 'Camp Texico on the Go!' (Amarillo, El Paso, Corrales, then a family camp at Bonita Park).",
  "'Equipping Texico / Equipando Texico' is a 2026 series of regional weekend trainings for local church leaders (Albuquerque Jan, El Paso Apr in Spanish and English, Midland/Odessa Oct, West Texas Dec) - the main pastoral-leadership initiative.",
  "Strong Hispanic youth federation (FESJA Texico, 20th anniversary Mar 2026, twice-yearly weekends at Bonita Park); a Filipino convocation (Oct 2026) and the union Asian-Pacific convocation are also listed.",
  "Item listed without description and not categorised beyond 'other': Albuquerque Balloon Fiesta (Oct 3-11, 2026).",
  "Southwestern Union Record stories (43 Texico stories since mid-Sep 2025) add a conference ACS flood-relief event in Ruidoso (May 26, 2026, 31 households helped with grants), a Spanish children's convocation (Apr 11, 2026) and local-church evangelism (two North Valley Spanish church series, Abilene youth sharing The Great Controversy with Kinyarwanda-speaking families). These are the only evangelism and community-service events found for Texico, and none appears on the conference calendar."
 ]
